	(text_box "I2C Pull Up\n================\nUsing 2x 10k pull-ups for the I2C lines (5k effective) instead of a single 4.7k,\nsince 10k is already used elsewhere on the board (single BOM value).\nPull-ups are placed at opposite ends of the bus to distribute the pull-up across it.\nThey are tied to the 3.3V power rail for the RP2040 to reduce the power usage when the camera is sleeping.\n"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 300.99 49.53 0)
		(size 105.41 16.2161)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type solid)
		)
		(fill
			(type color)
			(color 255 229 191 1)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "21eb52bf-53ff-4163-98cc-25cb50e68c35")
	)
	(text_box "RTC\n================\nWe are sing a PCF8563T on address 0x51 for the RTC\n- The crystal is a FC-135 that requires a load capacitance of 12.5pF\n- To tune the crystal we want 25pF on OSCI, we use a 22pF and will have about 2pF from stray capacitance to ground.\n- Battery backup is provided with a MS621FE-FL11E 3V Lithium Battery.\n- Charge limited through 1k resistor.\n- 5.5mAh Capacity, at 0.3uA that gives a backup life of over 700 days.\n- Sensing is done through a diode to prevent back powering the ATtiny when the device is off. Will slightly affect the ADC reading but gives a good enough idea."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 300.99 175.26 0)
		(size 105.41 24.3946)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type solid)
		)
		(fill
			(type color)
			(color 255 229 191 1)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "6352ca91-d8cf-492f-b433-400e52cc0c83")
	)
	(text_box "Temperature and Humidity Sensor\n================\nThe AHT20 is used as the temperature and humidity sensor. It uses the I2C Address 0x38"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 300.99 88.9778 0)
		(size 105.41 8.0376)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type solid)
		)
		(fill
			(type color)
			(color 255 229 191 1)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "a44ed84d-d892-498a-8011-a8cdc602ffde")
	)
	(text_box "Microphone Connector\n================\nThis 6 pin connector connects to the microphone PCB. The Micphone PCB is mounted to this PCB through the 2 mounting holes.\n"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 300.99 12.7 0)
		(size 105.41 10.0822)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type solid)
		)
		(fill
			(type color)
			(color 255 229 191 1)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "b4f76727-0ed8-4493-8054-083f4adf6d68")
	)
	(text_box "EEPROM\n================\nWe use a 2K EEPROM on address 0x50 to store some info about the PCB. This will be programmed when the camera is put together.\nIt stores the Version of the PCBs, Date of constuction, UUID, and if it is an audio only device (no LEPTON module).\nIt can be programmed using a TC2030 connector."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 300.99 125.73 0)
		(size 105.41 16.2161)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type solid)
		)
		(fill
			(type color)
			(color 255 229 191 1)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "d76bd8f4-aa7e-4c82-b33b-aee7abdaafb1")
	)
